References: <30bceb85ccdffaa64be2221199f7193cb9699a01.camel@groupe-cyllene.com>

For bug #8106, based on pve-manager
9c3f5e5258f73f31e273493232a79d615fd9e072.
Requires the shared qemu-server and WebRTC API series. The browser viewer
and media service are supplied by a separate console package.

Expose the shared display checkbox, render node and D-Bus audio backend.
Use WebRTC in the existing Console tab and menu when the VM exports a
shared display and a console service is installed. Keep CPU noVNC available
and respect an administrator's explicit xterm console preference.
pveproxy serves the separately packaged viewer.

Validation: JavaScript lint/bundle build and full pve-manager package/tests;
real Chrome, authenticated PVE sessions, CPU and GL viewers, embedded and
popup in both orders. Tests used packages built from this exact source.

Review questions: checkbox placement, console preference and separate
viewer packaging. The proposed dbus-display key is shared with qemu-server.

Dmitry R (3):
  pveproxy: serve the page of a WebRTC console viewer
  ui: use WebRTC for displays with a shared bus and console service
  ui: configure the shared D-Bus display, render node and audio

